These five deities may be worshipped either in their images of small size or through symbolic objects such as शालग्राम (round black stone) for विष्णु, बाणलिङ्ग (of white quartz) for शिव, metallic stone for देवी, red stone for गणपति and sphaṭika (crystal) for सूर्य. Geometrical drawings (yantra) like square, hexagon or circle are also sometimes used to represent these deities.
These five deities are represented as associated with the five cosmic elements:
Gaṇapati with earth;
Śiva with water;
Devī with fire;
Sūrya with air;
Viṣṇu with ether.
